The cleanest fix is to mark `WebViewBridgeDelegate` methods `@MainActor` (they already run on the main thread because WKScriptMessageHandler delivers on main) and call directly without Task wrapping. If cross-cutting changes to the protocol are out of scope for this task, add a comment pointing to the ordering caveat and consider replacing `Task { @MainActor in ... }` with `MainActor.assumeIsolated { ... }` (Swift 5.9+) which preserves call-site ordering and synchronicity:
```swift
func bridge(_ bridge: WebViewBridge, didRequestInsightDeepDive sessionId: String, topicIndex: Int) {
    MainActor.assumeIsolated {
        self.parent.workspaceManager.didRequestInsightDeepDive(sessionId: sessionId, topicIndex: topicIndex)
    }
}
```
